1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:02,301
Creators make the posts we all scroll

2
00:00:02,321 --> 00:00:04,716
past. The money goes to the platform,

3
00:00:04,736 --> 00:00:06,388
and the fans who found them first

4
00:00:06,408 --> 00:00:07,923
get nothing for it.

5
00:00:08,023 --> 00:00:10,549
Juno turns every post into a market.

6
00:00:10,624 --> 00:00:12,090
Post a photo or a reel,

7
00:00:12,110 --> 00:00:13,622
and it launches its own coin on

8
00:00:13,642 --> 00:00:14,806
a bonding curve,

9
00:00:14,826 --> 00:00:16,168
on Monad.

10
00:00:16,268 --> 00:00:18,396
Fans buy in as they scroll,

11
00:00:18,416 --> 00:00:20,953
and the creator earns the trading fees.

12
00:00:21,028 --> 00:00:22,378
When a curve fills,

13
00:00:22,398 --> 00:00:24,549
the post opens its own Kuru order

14
00:00:24,569 --> 00:00:25,434
book.

15
00:00:25,534 --> 00:00:27,650
It works because Monad is fast enough

16
00:00:27,670 --> 00:00:28,800
to trade at the speed of a

17
00:00:28,820 --> 00:00:32,434
feed: blocks every three hundred milliseconds,

18
00:00:32,454 --> 00:00:34,654
final in about half a second.

19
00:00:34,983 --> 00:00:36,182
This is the live app,

20
00:00:36,202 --> 00:00:37,764
on Monad testnet.

21
00:00:38,025 --> 00:00:39,804
These are Monad's real blocks,

22
00:00:39,824 --> 00:00:41,035
going from proposed,

23
00:00:41,055 --> 00:00:42,579
to voted, to finalized,

24
00:00:42,599 --> 00:00:45,171
about three hundred milliseconds apart.

25
00:00:46,171 --> 00:00:47,498
The feed is posts,

26
00:00:47,518 --> 00:00:49,370
and every post is a market.

27
00:00:49,503 --> 00:00:50,307
On a laptop,

28
00:00:50,327 --> 00:00:53,341
Monad's live activity sits right beside it.

29
00:00:54,341 --> 00:00:55,531
No wallet yet?

30
00:00:55,606 --> 00:00:57,665
One passkey prompt makes an account,

31
00:00:57,685 --> 00:00:59,708
through Mera. No seed phrase,

32
00:00:59,728 --> 00:01:01,278
and no extension.

33
00:01:02,278 --> 00:01:04,058
Tap Buy. The sheet gives a new

34
00:01:04,078 --> 00:01:06,472
wallet testnet MON from Juno's faucet,

35
00:01:06,492 --> 00:01:08,075
right here. Pick a size,

36
00:01:08,095 --> 00:01:09,169
and buy.

37
00:01:13,676 --> 00:01:15,514
Executed in one round trip,

38
00:01:15,534 --> 00:01:16,860
and final a moment later,

39
00:01:16,880 --> 00:01:18,152
measured on Monad.

40
00:01:18,285 --> 00:01:20,065
It cost a fraction of a cent,

41
00:01:20,085 --> 00:01:22,201
next to the same gas on Ethereum.

42
00:01:22,221 --> 00:01:23,757
And every receipt is a card you

43
00:01:23,777 --> 00:01:24,932
can post.

44
00:01:25,932 --> 00:01:28,130
The passkey itself is checked by Monad's

45
00:01:28,150 --> 00:01:30,547
own P256 precompile.

46
00:01:31,662 --> 00:01:33,816
This post filled its curve.

47
00:01:33,949 --> 00:01:36,530
It graduated into its own Kuru market,

48
00:01:36,550 --> 00:01:37,888
seeded from its raise,

49
00:01:37,908 --> 00:01:39,978
and its trades now fill on Kuru's

50
00:01:39,998 --> 00:01:41,154
order book.

51
00:01:43,924 --> 00:01:46,342
The same wallet trades perps on Perpl,

52
00:01:46,362 --> 00:01:49,039
with Agora's AUSD as margin.

53
00:01:49,114 --> 00:01:51,950
One tap brings ten thousand test AUSD

54
00:01:51,970 --> 00:01:53,532
from Agora's faucet.

55
00:01:53,665 --> 00:01:55,723
Deposit it into a Perpl account,

56
00:01:55,743 --> 00:01:57,708
open a two times long on Bitcoin,

57
00:01:57,728 --> 00:01:58,745
and close it.

58
00:01:59,098 --> 00:02:01,110
Every step is a real transaction on

59
00:02:01,130 --> 00:02:02,146
Monad.

60
00:02:04,113 --> 00:02:06,345
Pre-IPO trackers, like OpenAI,

61
00:02:06,365 --> 00:02:07,982
are marked against Tessera,

62
00:02:08,002 --> 00:02:10,049
and their net asset value is attested

63
00:02:10,069 --> 00:02:13,326
on chain by a Chainlink CRE workflow.

64
00:02:15,475 --> 00:02:18,183
Juno. Every post is a market,

65
00:02:18,203 --> 00:02:20,044
live on Monad testnet.
